-## Part 2 — Blocking side issues (fix alongside)
-
-**B-5.** Lemma 2.2(ii) final display: $\|L^{-1}g\|^2\le d^2\cdot4\|g\|^2$
-implies $\|L^{-1}\|\le2d$; the text prints $4d$ (display) and $2\sqrt d$
-(text + lemma header + §1 + conclusion + remark 3.6). Mechanical but global
-(five sites).
-
-**B-6.** Sign convention: `problem.tex` has source $=1$ with $u=0$ on
-$\partial D$; the document's $u_0=(1-|x|^2)/(2d)$ satisfies
-$\operatorname{div}(f\nabla u_0)=-1$, i.e. $u_0$ and every $u_f$ used are
-solutions for source $-1$ (equivalently $u\mapsto-u$). Since
-$f\mapsto u_f^{(+1)}=-u_f^{(-1)}$ and all estimates/rates use $\|u_{f_1}-u_{f_2}\|$,
-the mathematics is unaffected, but the document currently contradicts
-`problem.tex` where it writes $\Delta u_0=-1$ and uses the positive
-barrier. **Fix:** take $u_0=(|x|^2-1)/(2d)$, $\nabla u_0=x/d$,
-$\operatorname{div}(g\nabla u_0)=+(g+\frac{x\cdot\nabla}{d}g)=Lg$, define
-$\widetilde T=\Delta^{-1}\circ\operatorname{div}(\cdot\nabla u_0)=-T$,
-replace $T$ by $\widetilde T$ throughout (all norms unchanged), and fix the
-comparison-principle barrier sign in Lemma 2.2. (One-line change in
-Lemma 2.1's display; the Fourier packet analysis uses $|Tg|$ only.)
-
-**B-7.** "bounded isomorphism of $L^2(D)$" (Lemma 2.2(iii), §1 mechanism
-paragraph, Remark `rem:crux`) is false for the unbounded operator $L$
-(coefficients $x/d$ bounded but derivative not). **Fix:** state precisely:
-$L$ is *boundedly invertible* on $L^2$ (two-sided inverse $J$,
-$\|J\|\le2d$); $L:H^1\to L^2$ bounded ($\|Lg\|_2\le\|g\|_2+\frac1d\|\nabla g\|_2$);
-the useful operator-level statements for $T$ are
-$T\in\mathcal B(L^2,H^1_0)$ and $T\in\mathcal B(H^{-1},L^2)$, the latter via
-$Tg=\frac1d\Delta^{-1}\operatorname{div}(xg)$ (integration by parts, any
-$g\in L^2$; $xh\in H^{-1}$ continuously for $h\in H^{-1}$-spline sieves).
-Also remove "$L$ a bounded isomorphism" from the §1 "mechanism" sentence
-(the mechanism survives verbatim with "boundedly invertible").
-
-**B-8.** §5(C) duplicated sentence fragment around the fine-bias display
-("…and does not worsen the bound) by $P_\delta$ and does not worsen the
-estimate)"). Delete the duplicate.
