-## MG-12 (G1). The §5(C) risk analysis is vacuous as written; the displayed basic inequality cannot close at the minimax scale
-
-**Where.** Section (C), from "the standard quadratic-comparison manipulation"
-through the interpolated dichotomy paragraph.
-
-**What's wrong — three independent defects.**
-
-(a) **Wrong comparison object / structural $r\|h\|_2$ term.** The estimator
-is $L^2$-sieve least squares on the *nonlinear* forward map. With
-$e=\Pi_\delta f_0-f_0$ and $h=\widehat f-\Pi_\delta f_0$, the text writes
-$u_{\widehat f}-u_{f_0}=T(h+e)+\rho_{\widehat f}$ — i.e. it linearizes at
-$\one$, not at the comparison point. Lemma 2.4 gives
-$\|R(h)\|_2\lesssim\|h\|_\infty\|h\|_2$ only for the deviation about $\one$
-with force $\operatorname{div}((g-\one)\nabla u_0)$; applied with $g-\one$
-of full size $\asymp r$, the remainder *relative to the $h$-perturbation* is
-of order $r\|h\|_2$ — exactly the term the document itself produces in the
-displayed inequality
-$$c\delta\|h\|_2\ \lesssim\ n^{-1/2}\|\xi_\delta\|_2+\delta^\alpha+r(\|h\|_2+r).$$
-For this to yield $\|h\|_2\lesssim\delta^{-1}\cdot(\text{noise}+\text{bias})$
-one needs $r(\|h\|_2+r)$ to be $o(\delta\|h\|_2)$ — i.e. $r\lesssim\delta$,
-which fails catastrophically since $r$ is fixed and $\delta\to0$. The very
-inequality the document displays cannot support the next display; the
-subsequent "interpolation/dichotomy" paragraph treats a *different*
-($\|h\|_\infty$-controlled) remainder and never reconciles the two. **The
-proof as written does not show anything.**
-
-(b) **Compact sieve is not what is defined.** The sieve was defined as a
-wavelet/B-spline space "intersected with $\F(\alpha,r)$"; the later
-"compact sieve $\subset\{\|\cdot\|_{C^\alpha}\le2r\}$" appears without
-adjustment; worse, the interpolation
-$\|h\|_\infty\lesssim\|h\|_2^\theta(4r)^{1-\theta}$ is then *fixed* by the
-class ($\theta=\frac\alpha{\alpha+d/2}$, $\|h\|_\infty\lesssim\|h\|_2^{2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}$).
-
-(c) **The dichotomy's first regime rests on a false step.** With the fixed
-interpolation above, the absorption ratio is
-$\delta^{-1}\|h\|_\infty\lesssim\delta^{-1}\|h\|_2^{2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}$,
-whose exponent $2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)\,\alpha\text{-threshold}$ is
-$2\alpha^2>2\alpha+d$, i.e. **$\alpha>d/2$** — and the text asserts "the
-required condition reduces to $\alpha>1$." For $1<\alpha\le d/2$ (all of
-$d\ge3$, $\alpha$ near 1) the claimed $\delta_*^{(\alpha-1)\theta'}\to0$
-**does not exist**. As written, for generic $(\alpha,d)$ the absorption
-fails even granting (a) away. The dichotomy's second regime is also
-non-quantitative ("cannot balance unless $\|h\|_2\lesssim\delta_*^\alpha$" —
-true only *after* an absorption ratio has been established).
 
-**Repair sketch** (singular, directive — full text in Part 3, step 2):
-(i) replace $T$ on the sieve by a **uniform-in-$r$ smooth surrogate** $S$:
-solve $\operatorname{div}(m\nabla v)=0$ in $D$, $v=-\frac{1-|x|^2}{2d(1+r)}$
-on $\partial D$ ($m=\sum m_k(e_k\cdot\nabla)$, gap-free coefficients
-$m_k$, $m_0\ge1-2r$), requiring only $\Pi_\delta f_0,\widehat f$ in the
-closed $r$-ball, with $\|S h\|_{H^1}\lesssim\|h\|_2$ and
-$\|S h\|_2\gtrsim\delta\|h\|_2$ on annulus-supported sieve elements —
-proved *via the same Lax–Milgram/elliptic regularity already in the
-document*, no $\alpha>1$ needed at order zero;
-(ii) **remove the $r(\|h\|_2+r)$ display entirely**; linearize the PDE about
-the surrogate: $u_{g}=v+S(g-m)+\text{quadratic}$ with
-$\|\text{quad}\|_2\lesssim r\,\|g-m\|_2$ — the smallness now comes from the
-*elliptic modulus* $r$ times a quadratic, so the remainder-relative-to-$h$
-is $O(r\|h\|_2)$ **with $r$ chosen small at the start**
-($r\le c_0$ absorbing into $\tfrac c2\delta\|h\|_2$ where $c_0$ is
-$\delta$-independent if $h$ is annulus-supported and $\gtrsim$ constants are
-mode-wise — G2);
-(iii) for the $\|h\|_\infty^{(\alpha-1)/\alpha}$ second-order term, use the
-**scale-aware (Nikolskii-with-class-cap) bound**
-$\|h\|_\infty\lesssim\min\{\delta^{-d/2}\|h\|_2,C_h r\}$ **summing shell by
-shell** ($\|h_j\|_\infty\lesssim\min\{2^{j d/2}\|h_ j\|_2,2^{-j\alpha}r\}$),
-which at the minimax scale yields the absorption ratio
-$\delta_*^{\alpha-1}\to0$ **using only $\alpha>1$** — this is the step the
-"dichotomy" paragraph was reaching for and never wrote;
-(iv) pop the induction from the uniform-in-$g$ modulus: the linearized map
-$u_g-u_{f_0}$ on the $r$-ball is $O(r)$ away from $S$; the optimal
-local-linear rate is inherited from the Fano-based minimax comparison
-(standard modulus-of-continuity inheritance: the rate is the largest scale
-at which quadratic ≪ linear signal, i.e. exactly
-$\kappa\delta^{\alpha-1}\to0$). All steps are standard ingredients; none is
-circular; the final rate is unchanged. **Log-free upper bound is delivered**
-by the existing linear-functional observation once (i)–(iii) are in place
-(the $L^2$-normalized noise $\|\xi_\delta\|_2$ is $\chi^2$-concentrated;
-squared risks follow by $\E\|\xi_\delta\|_2^2=\delta^{-d}$).
