-**What's wrong — three independent defects.**
-
-(a) **Wrong comparison object / structural $r\|h\|_2$ term.** The estimator
-is $L^2$-sieve least squares on the *nonlinear* forward map. With
-$e=\Pi_\delta f_0-f_0$ and $h=\widehat f-\Pi_\delta f_0$, the text writes
-$u_{\widehat f}-u_{f_0}=T(h+e)+\rho_{\widehat f}$ — i.e. it linearizes at
-$\one$, not at the comparison point. Lemma 2.4 gives
-$\|R(h)\|_2\lesssim\|h\|_\infty\|h\|_2$ only for the deviation about $\one$
-with force $\operatorname{div}((g-\one)\nabla u_0)$; applied with $g-\one$
-of full size $\asymp r$, the remainder *relative to the $h$-perturbation* is
-of order $r\|h\|_2$ — exactly the term the document itself produces in the
-displayed inequality
-$$c\delta\|h\|_2\ \lesssim\ n^{-1/2}\|\xi_\delta\|_2+\delta^\alpha+r(\|h\|_2+r).$$
-For this to yield $\|h\|_2\lesssim\delta^{-1}\cdot(\text{noise}+\text{bias})$
-one needs $r(\|h\|_2+r)$ to be $o(\delta\|h\|_2)$ — i.e. $r\lesssim\delta$,
-which fails catastrophically since $r$ is fixed and $\delta\to0$. The very
-inequality the document displays cannot support the next display; the
-subsequent "interpolation/dichotomy" paragraph treats a *different*
-($\|h\|_\infty$-controlled) remainder and never reconciles the two. **The
-proof as written does not show anything.**
